diff --git a/docs/terrain-update-contract.md b/docs/terrain-update-contract.md
index 3b9c30ee..13bf8988 100644
--- a/docs/terrain-update-contract.md
+++ b/docs/terrain-update-contract.md
@@ -87,3 +87,25 @@ circular bitplane scrolling.
 
 Scene-verification builds compare the selected sequence with an independent
 full-record scan before drawing; normal and profiling builds omit that oracle.
+
+## Prepared terrain placement experiment
+
+`TERRAIN_WORDS=1` selects a host-prepared word bank for unmirrored sprite 51
+only. The retained generic renderer remains the fallback and reference. This
+changes placement, not terrain selection, order, invalidation, or ring ownership.
+All 26 source frames are 16×16 with origin (8,8), but their ordinary display
+position has a six-pixel word offset. They are not opaque: the union of the
+two colour planes is their write mask, including opaque palette-black pen 3.
+
+`generate-amiga-terrain-words.py` prepares mask/low/high words for each of the
+16 horizontal phases, after checking the planar pack and original input hashes.
+The immutable bank costs 79,888 bytes of ordinary executable data, with no
+additional Chip allocation or runtime pixel conversion. Each placement applies
+the viewport edge masks and copies prepared colour words under coverage;
+vertical clipping advances the source rows and ring wrapping resets the
+destination. Non-tile decorations and mirrored assets use the existing path.
+
+`make test-amiga-terrain-words` compares complete plane buffers and guard bytes
+with the generic renderer for every frame and phase, both layer targets, screen
+and viewport edges, one-pixel clips and wrapped origins. This is a pixel and
+memory-boundary gate, not evidence that the experiment meets its timing target.
